 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Property of the isomorphism-near-closure construction, [stacks-project]",
 "statement": "If $U\\to V$ is an isomorphism over an open neighbourhood of $T$, then\n$\\mathsf{IsoBl}_{V,T}(q)\\to X$ is $V$-admissible and the strict transform\nof $q$ is an isomorphism over an open neighbourhood of the closure of $T$\nin $\\mathsf{IsoBl}_{V,T}(q)$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-near-closure/lemma-nagata-isomorphism-near-closure.md",
  "place": "node lemma-nagata-isomorphism-near-closure, order 260"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By [lemma-nagata-maximal-isomorphism-open], the assumed isomorphism\nneighbourhood is contained in $\\operatorname{IsoOpen}(U\\to V)$; hence the\nbad locus $E$ is disjoint from $T$. The two separation steps make\n$\\overline T_c$ and $\\overline E_c$\ndisjoint in $X_1$, so $X_0$ contains an open neighbourhood of\n$\\overline T_c$, hence of $\\overline T$. On\n$V\\setminus E_c$ the restricted proper map is already an isomorphism.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-maximal-isomorphism-open"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "By [lemma-nagata-elimination-indeterminacy], the strict transform after\nthe constructed blow-up of $X_0$ is an open immersion. The strict transform\nis proper because it is a closed subscheme of the base change of the proper\nmorphism $q$ (use the closed-chart model in\n[prop-nagata-strict-transform-closed-fiber-product]); hence\n[lemma-nagata-proper-open-dense-iso] applies once density is checked.\nThe open $V\\setminus E_c$ is scheme-theoretically dense in $X_0$ by the\ndensity-preservation clause for admissible blow-ups, and its pullback is the\npreserved isomorphism open by\n[lemma-nagata-strict-transform-over-complement]. Thus the strict\ntransform over $X_0$ is an isomorphism. The extension construction has\nunit center on $X_1\\setminus X_0$ and restricts canonically to the preceding\nblow-up on $X_0$ by\n[lemma-nagata-extend-admissible-blowup]; the restriction and inverse\nmaps therefore transport across the canonical strict-transform comparison.\nSince $\\overline T\\subset X_0$, this transported isomorphism holds on an\nopen neighbourhood of $\\overline T$. Finally\n[lemma-nagata-admissible-blowup-comp] identifies the composite with one\n$V$-admissible blow-up, giving the asserted construction.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-elimination-indeterminacy",
    "prop-nagata-strict-transform-closed-fiber-product",
    "lemma-nagata-proper-open-dense-iso",
    "lemma-nagata-strict-transform-over-complement",
    "lemma-nagata-extend-admissible-blowup",
    "lemma-nagata-admissible-blowup-comp"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
